GROUP(5)                       P32W Unix                        GROUP(5)

NAME
       group - group file

SYNOPSIS
       #include <grp.h>

DESCRIPTION
       /etc/group names the groups, one line each, four fields
       separated by colons:

              name:password:gid:member,member,...

       name       the group's name
       password   unused; leave it empty
       gid        the numeric group id
       members    login names, separated by commas

       The file as shipped:

              root::0:root
              staff::10:ken
              guest::20:guest

       A user's group is the gid field of /etc/passwd (see
       passwd(5)); login(1) sets it. getgrnam and getgrgid (see
       getgrent(3)) read this file, so that ls(1), id(1), chown(1),
       tar(1) and adduser(8) can show and take group names.

FILES
       /etc/group

SEE ALSO
       passwd(5), getgrent(3), id(1), ls(1), chown(1), adduser(8)

BUGS
       The member lists are not used: P32W Unix has no supplementary
       groups (a process has one group id) and no newgrp. Only the
       first 31 members of a line are returned. Lines longer than
       255 characters are cut short, and # comments are not
       recognised.
